Topic: Top Real-World MLOps Interview Questions for DevOps & SRE Engineers

As the tech landscape shifts toward AI-driven automation, MLOps has become one of the most in-demand skillsets in cloud and DevOps roles.
 If you’re preparing for an interview or transitioning from DevOps/SRE into MLOps, these scenario-based questions will help you sharpen your fundamentals 👇

Top MLOps Interview Questions
What is MLOps and how does it extend traditional DevOps principles?
How does the MLOps lifecycle differ from the software development lifecycle (SDLC)?
What are the key components of an MLOps pipeline?
Explain the CI/CD/CD concept in MLOps (Continuous Integration / Continuous Delivery / Continuous Deployment).
What tools are commonly used in MLOps workflows?
How do you automate model training and deployment?
What’s the role of version control in MLOps for datasets and models?
How do you manage model drift in production?
What is feature store in MLOps, and why is it important?
How can you monitor model performance after deployment?
What’s the difference between model retraining and model fine-tuning?
How do you deploy ML models using Docker and Kubernetes?
What’s the difference between online and batch inference?
How do you integrate model serving frameworks like TensorFlow Serving or TorchServe?
What is the purpose of MLflow, and how does it help in MLOps pipelines?
How do you ensure data quality and integrity in the MLOps pipeline?
Explain the concept of data versioning. Which tools are used for it?
What are some challenges in scaling MLOps in a multi-cloud or hybrid environment?
How do you handle model governance, compliance, and auditability?
What are the key differences between Kubeflow, MLflow, and SageMaker?
How can you use Airflow for orchestrating ML workflows?
How do you implement security and access control in MLOps pipelines?
What are the common metrics to evaluate ML model performance in production?
How do you handle rollback or redeployment if a new model version performs poorly?
What are the best practices for building production-ready MLOps pipelines?

Pro Tip:
 MLOps is not just about models — it’s about reliability, automation, and scalability of ML systems.
 If you already know DevOps, SRE, and Cloud, you’re 70% ready for MLOps. The rest is mastering data, model training, and deployment automation.
